  "body": "Stacked on #3990. This branch starts from `issue/1120-theme-colour-tokens` (the guard). Its own commit is the last one (55001e555). Review that commit; the two commits before it are #3990. Merge #3990 first.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe first family of #1120: the viewport handle and pick inks.\n\n- Three colour tokens join `Tokens` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme.rs`). Each is also a theme-file key (`colors.<name>`, `theme_files::COLOR_NAMES`):\n\n  | Token | Draws | Was |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | `handle_shade` | the shadow under a move or turn handle and under its readout | `Color32::from_black_alpha(170)` |\n  | `handle_text` | the readout text of a handle, and the fallback ink of an axis | `Color32::WHITE` |\n  | `pick_rim` | the rim of a picked point's disc | `Color32::from_rgb(245, 240, 250)` |\n\n- Both built-in tables (`theme/tables.rs`) carry the old values, so no pixel changes. The light table keeps the dark values: the handles and the picks draw over the 3D view, not over the chrome.\n- The draw sites read `theme::current()`: `egui_app/move_handles.rs`, `egui_app/turn_handles.rs`, `align_pick_viz.rs`.\n- The colour-literal guard (`crates/ui/tests/colour_literals.rs`) loses the rows of those three files. The row of `theme/tables.rs` goes from 32 to 38 (3 tokens in 2 tables).\n- Wiring of the new keys: `theme_files/names.rs`, `theme_files/overlay.rs`, `assets/themes/theme.json.example`, and the colour table of `docs/user-guide/themes.md`.\n- `geom_legal` and its two const asserts move unchanged from `theme.rs` (425 lines) to the new `theme/legal.rs`. `theme.rs` is now 318 lines.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1120-handle-inks.md` (flat names, the light column, what was dropped).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `theme_viewport_inks::the_built_in_columns_keep_the_handle_and_pick_colours` (new file `crates/ui/tests/theme_viewport_inks.rs`): both columns carry the old literals.\n- `theme_viewport_inks::a_theme_file_sets_each_handle_and_pick_ink_by_name`: a theme file sets the three keys, with no \"unknown key\" note.\n- `theme_example::example_has_exactly_the_loader_keys`: the example file has the three new keys.\n- `colour_literals::no_colour_literal_outside_the_allowed_rows`: the three files have no colour literal left.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the head 55001e555:\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 12 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (2.5 min). It includes `ui suites: lib`, `ui suites: colour_literals`, `ui suites: theme_example`, `ui suites: theme_files` and `ui suites: theme_viewport_inks`.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none (`cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run`: 0 steps reached).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI and no screenshot. The values are the old ones; the test pins them.\n- The shipped themes `teal-night.json` and `horizon-day.json` do not set the new keys. They take the values of their base table, as before.\n\nChangelog: Themes can set the viewport handle shadow, the handle readout text and the rim of a picked point (`handle_shade`, `handle_text`, `pick_rim`).\n\nRefs #1120\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
